  "worked_solution": "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\u2308x\u2309$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\u2308x\u2309=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.4) & =\u2308\\sqrt{\\frac{0.4}{2.5}}\u2309 \\\\  & =\u2308\\sqrt{0.16}\u2309 \\\\  & =\u23080.4\u2309.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\u23080.4\u2309=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.4) & =\u23080.4\u2309 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
